hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"168","Subḥāna alladhī yusabbiḥu al-raʿdu bi-ḥamdihi, wa al-malāʾikatu min khīfatihi.. Glory be to Him whom the thunder glorifies with His praise, and the angels do so out of fear of Him."
"169","Allāhumma sqinā ghaythan mughīthan marī'an murī'an, nāfi'an ghayra ḍārin, ājilan ghayra ājilin.. O Allah, grant us rain that is beneficial, wholesome, and abundant, useful and not harmful, immediate and not delayed."
